Benefits to the ecosystem	
This session introduces a practical, Kubernetes-native pattern for running agentic AI workloads with low latency and high reliability. By combining warm pools, checkpoint/restore, and controlled upgrade semantics, it reduces cold-start times, minimizes failed or duplicated work during retries, and enables safe, iterative runtime evolution without disrupting active sessions.

Attendees will gain reusable control-loop patterns (warm pool management, high-throughput claiming, checkpoint lifecycle, and revision gating) that can be applied across platforms. These approaches improve cluster efficiency, lower infrastructure costs, and standardize how stateful AI sessions are handled in cloud-native environments—helping teams build more responsive, fault-tolerant, and production-ready AI systems on Kubernetes.